Package: @PACKAGE_ID@
Name: uutils coreutils
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCHITECTURE@
Description: GNU coreutils rewritten in Rust, for jailbroken iOS
 The uutils reimplementation of the GNU core utilities -- ls, cp, mv, cat,
 sort, dd, du and about a hundred more -- cross-compiled for iOS and packaged
 for both roothide and rootless bootstraps from one arm64 build. The
 architecture field says which layout this package is, not which CPU it runs
 on. Upstream is @UPSTREAM@.
 .
 This package does not replace the GNU coreutils your bootstrap ships: apt,
 dpkg and Sileo depend on that one, and their maintainer scripts run the very
 tools that would be swapped out. Everything here is installed side by side in
 @UTILS_PATH@ instead, and nothing is added to PATH.
 .
 To use it, put that directory first in PATH -- $UUTILS_BIN is exported for you
 by /etc/profile.d/uutils.sh, so a shell can opt in with
 `export PATH="$UUTILS_BIN:$PATH"` and opt back out by starting a new one. The
 whole set is also reachable without touching PATH at all: `coreutils ls -l`.
 .
 Every process these utilities start goes through posix_spawn(); there is no
 fork() in the binary, no setuid/setgid, and nothing escalates privilege:
 children inherit what the shell had. stdbuf, chroot, chcon and runcon are not
 included.
Maintainer: OwnGoal Studio <not-gonna-reply@owngoal.dev>
Author: uutils developers <https://github.com/uutils/coreutils>
Section: Utilities
Priority: optional
Depends: firmware (>= @MIN_IOS@)
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
